{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1775","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1775","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1775\",\"parent_revision\":\"686ef245eeef0c6771d3168f7e2f02dbe18141315f7a8033e3205edc7cb398d2\",\"root_revision\":\"686ef245eeef0c6771d3168f7e2f02dbe18141315f7a8033e3205edc7cb398d2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAppendTaskConfig (sam_schema/core/action_models.py:240) accepts task_yaml: str \u2014 a raw YAML string that is parsed and validated inside _sam_plan_append_task rather than at the MCP tool boundary. This means schema violations in the task payload are caught later in the call stack, not at the tool input layer where FastMCP/Pydantic can produce a clear structured error.\\n\\nThe problem: callers must serialize a TaskDefinition dict to YAML manually, then the server deserializes and validates it. This round-trip adds complexity and defers validation.\\n\\nThe desired outcome: AppendTaskConfig accepts a typed TaskDefinition (or an equivalent Pydantic model) directly, so Pydantic validates the task at the MCP boundary and callers pass a structured object instead of a raw YAML string.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- AppendTaskConfig is part of the public MCP tool interface (sam_plan action=append_task). Changing it is a breaking change for any caller that constructs task_yaml: str payloads.\\n- Must provide a migration path or backward-compat shim.\\n- The TaskDefinition TypedDict (task_backend_types.py:22) is the obvious target type, but TypedDict does not satisfy Pydantic's model validation directly \u2014 an equivalent Pydantic model may be needed.\\n- Investigate whether the current YAML string approach has any intentional benefits (e.g., supporting multi-document YAML or comments) before removing it.\\n\\nFlagged during review of commit fixing #1770 agent doc speculation bugs. The YAML-string design is a real API boundary smell worth addressing deliberately.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] CLI and MCP plan/task create, append, import/export, and bookend registration paths accept\\n      typed objects or JSON only; no caller must serialize a task, plan, T0 baseline, or TN\\n      verification record to YAML.\\n- [ ] CLI stdin plan/task authoring accepts JSON using the canonical field contract and rejects\\n      YAML with a structured error.\\n- [ ] Every agent/API input is validated through the canonical Pydantic model at the object\\n      boundary, with tests proving field-level errors for missing, invalid, and extra fields as\\n      defined by that model.\\n- [ ] Canonical plan/task/bookend serialization and deserialization round-trip through JSON without\\n      data loss, YAML aliases, YAML coercion, or file-path-derived identity.\\n- [ ] `ContentTaskProvider` and ledger/content projections accept canonical JSON only; malformed or\\n      non-JSON content fails explicitly and cannot fall back to YAML parsing.\\n- [ ] All authoritative legacy SAM plan/task records required after cutover are inventoried and\\n      converted before removal of compatibility code; the shipped runtime retains no indefinite\\n      YAML read, write, migration, or dual-read path.\\n- [ ] The plan/task YAML providers, Gist YAML layer, YAML plan index, readers, writers, detectors,\\n      normalizers, legacy import/routing, migration command, exports, factories, and dead callers\\n      are removed.\\n- [ ] File-oriented consumers no longer discover `.yaml` plans/tasks, parse or mutate task YAML\\n      frontmatter, use YAML paths as identities, or depend on local-YAML-only model fields.\\n- [ ] T0 and TN structured artifacts are JSON at registration and consumption boundaries and are\\n      validated against typed schemas at both boundaries.\\n- [ ] YAML-compatibility tests and fixtures are removed with the behavior they cover. Replacement\\n      tests cover JSON stdin, CLI/MCP parity, Pydantic validation failures, content persistence,\\n      ledger import/export, logical identity, and T0/TN JSON round trips.\\n- [ ] Skills, agents, command references, examples, README content, architecture documentation,\\n      and work-ledger documentation contain no instruction to construct, parse, store, migrate, or\\n      read SAM plan/task/bookend YAML.\\n- [ ] Plan/task/bookend runtime and documentation searches contain no YAML-only symbols or\\n      instructions outside a reviewed allowlist for the explicitly excluded YAML uses.\\n- [ ] Dependencies and helper code used only by the removed plan/task YAML paths are deleted; YAML\\n      libraries still required by excluded configuration or formats are not removed blindly.\\n- [ ] The development-harness test, lint, type-check, and cross-frontend parity gates pass.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Agent, CLI, and MCP authoring and ingestion\\n\\n- Make all plan/task creation, append, import/export, and structured bookend boundaries typed or\\n  JSON-only.\\n- Change `plan append-task --stdin` and any equivalent stdin/input paths to accept one JSON object\\n  using the canonical model fields.\\n- Remove YAML parsing and YAML-only conventions such as the `task:` ID/key path.\\n- Remove raw-dict normalization or aliases that exist only to accommodate YAML callers; retain\\n  normalization only where an active non-YAML contract demonstrably requires it.\\n\\n### Schema and validation boundaries\\n\\n- Validate incoming JSON objects directly through the canonical Pydantic models.\\n- Validate deserialized content before it enters domain operations or projections.\\n- Preserve structured validation errors with exact field locations and values.\\n- Remove YAML-specific coercion, comments, aliases, local-file source fields, and documentation\\n  from plan/task models where no active JSON/typed consumer requires them.\\n- Treat malformed or non-JSON canonical content as invalid data with a structured error; do not\\n  silently invoke a second parser.\\n\\n### Serialization, persistence, and providers\\n\\n- Keep JSON serialization in `ContentTaskProvider` and JSON/SQLite ledger state as the canonical\\n  persistence path.\\n- Remove legacy YAML fallback from plan-content parsing and ledger/content projection reads.\\n- Remove the plan/task YAML implementation and dead adapters, including the equivalent current\\n  surfaces for `LocalYamlTaskProvider`, `GistTaskLayer`, YAML `PlanIdIndex`, YAML\\n  readers/writers/detection/normalization, legacy YAML import/routing, `plan migrate`, and their\\n  public exports and callers.\\n- Convert authoritative legacy records exactly once before the runtime cutover. The delivered\\n  runtime must not retain a YAML migration, dual-read, or write-through compatibility path.\\n- Preserve provider-neutral logical plan/task identity and the backend capabilities established\\n  by #912.\\n\\n### Consumers and structured artifacts\\n\\n- Replace `.yaml` plan/task file discovery, file-path identity, YAML-frontmatter task\\n  parsing/mutation, and local-YAML status mapping with logical plan/task addresses and typed\\n  CLI/MCP reads.\\n- Update implementation-manager and verification consumers to operate on canonical records rather\\n  than local YAML files.\\n- Represent T0 baseline and TN verification bookend artifacts as JSON and validate them against\\n  typed schemas before registration and again when consumed.\\n- Remove instructions and interfaces that ask an agent to assemble, parse-check, pass, or read a\\n  YAML string for those artifacts.\\n\\n### Tests, fixtures, dependencies, and documentation\\n\\n- Delete tests and fixtures whose contract is legacy plan/task or bookend YAML compatibility.\\n- Replace them with positive and negative JSON boundary, round-trip, persistence, and parity tests.\\n- Remove plan/task YAML helpers, imports, parser setup, and dependencies that become unused. A\\n  repository dependency used by unrelated in-scope-excluded YAML must remain available to those\\n  consumers.\\n- Update all affected skills, agents, command references, examples, README content, architecture\\n  documentation, and work-ledger documentation to describe the JSON/typed path only.\\n- Remove fabricated `.yaml` paths and any wording that presents YAML as the plan/task data model.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSAM now has typed Pydantic plan/task models, JSON content records, JSON CLI output, and a SQLite\\nwork ledger, but it still maintains YAML authoring, parsing, normalization, legacy persistence,\\nmigration, consumer, test, and documentation paths around those same records.\\n\\nAgents currently serialize structured plan, task, or bookend data to YAML in several workflows\\nonly for the system to parse it back into typed objects, JSON, or SQL-backed state. This duplicate\\nrepresentation:\\n\\n- consumes agent context and output tokens;\\n- duplicates serialization, parsing, normalization, and validation code;\\n- expands fixtures, tests, documentation, dependencies, and maintenance work;\\n- permits YAML-specific aliases, paths, and coercions to leak into the domain model; and\\n- creates format-specific failure modes without providing a required human or runtime capability.\\n\\nThe original scope of this issue was a typed `AppendTaskConfig`/`CreatePlanConfig` refactor. That\\nboundary is already typed: `CreatePlanConfig.tasks` is `list[TaskDefinition]`,\\n`AppendTaskConfig.task` is `TaskDefinition`, and the MCP handlers consume those values without\\nparsing YAML. The remaining problem is the full YAML lifecycle around those typed objects.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Desired Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSAM plan/task and structured T0/TN bookend data use one representation chain:\\n\\n```text\\nagent / CLI / MCP JSON -> Pydantic validation -> typed Python object -> JSON content or SQLite\\n```\\n\\n- Agents and API clients send structured objects/JSON, never YAML strings or YAML-shaped files.\\n- Pydantic validates records at object boundaries and returns structured field-level errors.\\n- Runtime content serialization and deserialization use JSON only.\\n- Durable state remains in the existing backend-native content and SQLite/JSON paths.\\n- Human-readable state is obtained through CLI/MCP queries over those canonical records.\\n- No shipped SAM plan/task or bookend path authors, parses, detects, normalizes, stores, migrates,\\n  or documents YAML.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Relationship To 912\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRelated foundation: #912.\\n\\n#912 establishes backend-native durable storage through the `TaskBackend` abstraction, but its\\nscope explicitly retains `LocalYamlTaskProvider`, Gist plan YAML, YAML plan indexes, dual-read\\nfallback, and indefinite legacy YAML reads. This issue completes the representation migration\\nleft behind by #912 while preserving the backend abstraction and backend-native storage\\ncapabilities delivered there.\\n\\nImplementation ordering is:\\n\\n1. Preserve and verify the backend-native JSON/content and SQLite paths established by #912.\\n2. Inventory and convert any authoritative legacy SAM plan/task records before cutover.\\n3. Remove the YAML providers, fallback, migration routes, and consumers in this issue.\\n\\nThis issue depends on the relevant backend-native storage foundation from #912, not on completion\\nof unrelated #912 work. If active #912 changes still modify the same storage surfaces, those\\nchanges land before this issue's destructive YAML cutover. Backward compatibility alone is not a\\nreason to retain a YAML reader, writer, dual-read path, or provider after the cutover.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Out Of Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis is not a repository-wide YAML ban. Do not remove or convert YAML whose purpose is unrelated\\nto SAM plan/task records or their structured T0/TN bookends, including:\\n\\n- `.dh/config.yaml` and other project or plugin configuration;\\n- skill/agent Markdown frontmatter;\\n- CI, pre-commit, and plugin manifests;\\n- backlog-provider caches and backlog issue fixtures;\\n- dispatch-schema or milestone-dispatch data; and\\n- research-document frontmatter and unrelated artifact formats.\\n\\n`ruamel.yaml` or another YAML dependency may remain when an out-of-scope consumer still requires\\nit. Verification must target the SAM plan/task/bookend paths and symbols, with a reviewed allowlist\\nfor unrelated YAML.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Verification Expectations\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nVerification must demonstrate the full representation boundary, not only absence of one parameter\\nname:\\n\\n1. Exercise agent-equivalent CLI and MCP create/append calls with JSON objects and compare their\\n   typed results.\\n2. Round-trip representative plan, task, T0, and TN records through their canonical JSON and\\n   persistence boundaries.\\n3. Submit malformed JSON and structurally invalid records and assert structured Pydantic errors;\\n   submit valid YAML syntax and assert that it is not accepted as plan/task input.\\n4. Read canonical provider content and ledger projections and prove no fallback parser is invoked.\\n5. Search runtime code, tests, fixtures, skills, agents, and documentation for the removed YAML\\n   symbols and instructions, reviewing each remaining match against the explicit exclusions.\\n6. Run the repository-prescribed development-harness test, lint, type-check, and cross-frontend\\n   parity gates.\\n\\n<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"790f8f7b19015484e065c89776a30cc007693125e1199212260c86d299c917a5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABWNd2pw\"}"}